title The three vendor names surveyed
prompt Keaton: I am deciding seating now that I want to molt and archive any files, rules and documents associated with ChatGPT, Cursor and/or Grok -- widened twice in the same sitting to include a breach and mitra shed prep of all old files, and to include arbor and the dotfile folders.
think A molt preps and opens no cut, and a survey is the named looking pass before the first GREEN. Keaton said he is DECIDING the seating, so the deliverable is the map he decides from -- not a sweep I chose the shape of.
think The living set is what a molt can touch. Tracked files whose basename carries no one-clock stamp and which sit outside date, archive and yonder: 6,499 of roughly 14,700. Everything else is testimony and keeps every word.
think Cursor 353 living files by the bare word and 135 by a strong editor marker; ChatGPT/Codex/OpenAI 66; Grok 9 of which three are incidental. The gap between 353 and 135 IS the first trap rather than noise.
think Ordered Lindy-first, crux-first: Grok is five edits and no guard moves; Codex is one lane with a shed already open; Cursor is structural and is one decision rather than many, because rule_twin, the 26 twin footers and the .cursor room stand or fall together.
obs THE WORD IS NOT THE THING, FOUR TIMES OVER, AND EACH TRAP WAS MEASURED RATHER THAN GUESSED. A sweep on the bare word breaks Brushstroke: edit_cursor.rye spells the capitalised type Cursor SEVENTEEN times and means the blinking caret. GROK is an ordinary English word standing at line 19 of the pinned four-letter list waymark_derive draws from, so editing that file re-draws seated waymarks. I had written the flw caution as a guess, measured it, read zero from a whole-line match, and nearly withdrew it -- the whole-line match was the wrong reading, and the word is there.
obs THE PUBLIC SEED ALREADY SCRUBS BOTH EDITOR ROOMS. template-manifest.bron reads scrub .cursor beside scrub .claude, so retiring .cursor changes nothing public. That lowers the risk and it also lowers the urgency, and both halves are worth saying to someone deciding.
obs THE CRUX IS SOURCE.md AND IT IS ALREADY DOUBLE-BOOKED. Fifty-eight Cursor mentions across 45,037 bytes, and Part One's stated end is a working, jailed Cursor -- so retiring Cursor rewrites the guide's spine. Keaton has ALSO named SOURCE and the first-hour tutorial for the fleet-insight refresh. Two jobs on one document is one job, and doing them apart rewrites the same bytes twice.
obs ONE QUESTION I WILL NOT ANSWER FOR HIM. gratitude/ is a thanks record and the licence discipline keeps what we learned from; archiving a gratitude page is a different act from retiring a tool. Named as a question rather than folded into a tier.
loom survey=living_set files=6499 tracked=14700 method=stamp-and-name
